{"unit_id":1,"stage_id":1,"lesson":{"lesson_id":13,"lesson_key":"S1L13","stage_id":1,"title":"Ma'rifah se Nakirah (1): الْكِتَابُ ← كِتَابٌ (Koi / Ek)","title_i18n":{"hinglish":"Ma'rifah se Nakirah (1): الْكِتَابُ ← كِتَابٌ (Koi / Ek)","en":"Definite to Indefinite (1): الْكِتَابُ ← كِتَابٌ (A / Any Book)","ur":"معرفہ سے نکرہ (۱): الْكِتَابُ ← كِتَابٌ (کوئی / ایک)","hi":"मारिफ़ा से नकिरा (1): الْكِتَابُ ← كِتَابٌ (कोई / एक)"},"arabic_Focus":"الْكِتَابُ ، الرَّسُولُ ← كِتَابٌ ، رَسُولٌ","hinglish_Focus":"Al-Kitaab (Khaas Kitaab) → Ek kitaab / Koi kitaab, Ek Rasool (Tanween ـٌ)","page_numbers":"38–39","book_page":38,"sections":[{"id":"sec_hero","type":"hero_header","data":{"arabic":"الْكِتَابُ ، الرَّسُولُ ← كِتَابٌ ، رَسُولٌ","hinglish":"Al-Kitaab (Khaas Kitaab) → Ek kitaab / Koi kitaab, Ek Rasool (Tanween ـٌ)","arabic_word":"الْكِتَابُ ، الرَّسُولُ","arabic_combined":"الْكِتَابُ ، الرَّسُولُ ← كِتَابٌ ، رَسُولٌ","hinglish_word":"Al-Kitaab (Khaas Kitaab)","hinglish_combined":"Al-Kitaab (Khaas Kitaab) → Ek kitaab / Koi kitaab, Ek Rasool (Tanween ـٌ)","title_en":"Ma'rifah se Nakirah (1): الْكِتَابُ ← كِتَابٌ (Koi / Ek)","subtitle":"Unit 1 • Lesson 13 (Book Page 38–39)","transformations":[{"before_ar":"الْكِتَابُ ، الرَّسُولُ","after_ar":"كِتَابٌ ، رَسُولٌ","before_hi":"Al-Kitaab (Khaas Kitaab)","after_hi":"Ek kitaab / Koi kitaab, Ek Rasool (Tanween ـٌ)"}]}},{"id":"sec_intro_table","type":"intro_table","data":{"title":"S1L13 — Ma'rifah se Nakirah (1): الْكِتَابُ ← كِتَابٌ (Koi / Ek): Buniyadi Misaalein","caption":"S1L13 — Ma'rifah se Nakirah (1): الْكِتَابُ ← كِتَابٌ (Koi / Ek): Buniyadi Misaalein","headers":["Qism / Qaa'ida","Arabi Misaal","Hinglish Mafhoom"],"rows":[["الْـ (Khaas) ← Tanween ـٌ (Aam)","الْكِتَابُ ← كِتَابٌ / الرَّسُولُ ← رَسُولٌ","Khaas kitaab -> Ek (koi) kitaab / Ek Rasool"],["Do Pesh (ـٌ) = 'Ek' ya 'Koi'","مَلِكٌ / أُمَّةٌ / آيَةٌ / مَغْفِرَةٌ","Ek badshah / Ek ummat / Ek nishani / Bakhshish"],["وَ ke saath Nakirah Jode","هُدًى وَشِفَاءٌ / هُدًى وَرَحْمَةٌ وَبُشْرَىٰ","Hidayat aur shifa / Hidayat, rahmat aur khushkhabri"]]}},{"id":"sec_s1l13_concept","type":"rule_paragraph","data":{"text":"<div class=\"lesson-concept-svg\" style=\"margin:14px 0;padding:12px;border-radius:12px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#0f172a,#1e293b);border:1px solid #334155;\">\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 760 190\" width=\"100%\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\">\n  <defs>\n    <linearGradient id=\"u123grad\" x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"1\" y2=\"1\">\n      <stop offset=\"0%\" stop-color=\"#0d9488\"/>\n      <stop offset=\"100%\" stop-color=\"#0284c7\"/>\n    </linearGradient>\n  </defs>\n  <rect x=\"8\" y=\"8\" width=\"744\" height=\"174\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#0f172a\" stroke=\"#1e293b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <rect x=\"22\" y=\"20\" width=\"150\" height=\"26\" rx=\"13\" fill=\"url(#u123grad)\"/>\n  <text x=\"97\" y=\"37\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">UNIT 1 • LESSON 13</text>\n  <text x=\"188\" y=\"38\" fill=\"#f8fafc\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"700\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">Ma'rifah se Nakirah (1): الْكِتَابُ ← كِتَابٌ (Koi / Ek) (Page 38–39)</text>\n  <rect x=\"24\" y=\"58\" width=\"220\" height=\"68\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#1e293b\" stroke=\"#475569\"/>\n  <text x=\"134\" y=\"98\" fill=\"#fbbf24\" font-size=\"24\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" direction=\"rtl\" font-family=\"Traditional Arabic,Amiri,serif\">الْكِتَابُ ، الرَّسُولُ</text>\n  <circle cx=\"288\" cy=\"92\" r=\"22\" fill=\"#0d9488\"/>\n  <text x=\"288\" y=\"98\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">Nakirah (Tanween ـٌ)</text>\n  <rect x=\"332\" y=\"58\" width=\"402\" height=\"68\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#0f292a\" stroke=\"#14b8a6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n  <text x=\"533\" y=\"98\" fill=\"#34d399\" font-size=\"23\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" direction=\"rtl\" font-family=\"Traditional Arabic,Amiri,serif\">كِتَابٌ ، رَسُولٌ</text>\n  <text x=\"26\" y=\"150\" fill=\"#cbd5e1\" font-size=\"12.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">• الْكِتَابُ ، الرَّسُولُ (Al-Kitaab (Khaas Kitaab)) → كِتَابٌ ، رَسُولٌ (Ek kitaab / Koi kitaab, Ek Rasool (Tanween ـٌ)).</text>\n  <text x=\"26\" y=\"170\" fill=\"#94a3b8\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">• Unit 1 mein aasaan Qur'ani alfaaz aur buniyadi ishaare/qawa'id sikhaye gaye hain.</text>\n</svg>\n</div>\n**Qaa'ida (Pages 38–39):** Jab kisi ism ke shuru se `الْـ` hata diya jaye toh uske aakhir par **Do Pesh (`ـٌ` Tanween)** aa jate hain, aur uske ma'ni mein **'ek' ya 'koi'** (*Nakirah*) ka mafhoom paida hota hai: `الْكِتَابُ` (woh kitaab) ← `كِتَابٌ` (ek kitaab / koi kitaab)."}},{"id":"sec_s1l13_lbl1","type":"section_label","data":{"text":"Darj zail misaalein dekhein (Darj zail misaalon par ghaur karein):"}},{"id":"sec_s1l13_r3","type":"rule_paragraph","data":{"text":"Upar diye gaye pehle column mein woh alfaaz hain jo aap pichhle asbaaq mein padh chuke hain. Doosre column mein wahi alfaaz thode se farq ke sath dobara aaye hain: unke shuru mein (الْـ) nahi hai aur aakhir mein tanween (ً ٍ ٌ) hai, jaise (كِتَابٌ). Jab koi lafz baghair (الْـ) ke istemaal hota hai, toh aam taur par uska mafhoom 'koi' ya 'ek' (ek / any) hota hai. Arabi mein aur Quran-e-Majeed mein aksar alfaaz (الْـ) se shuru hote hain. Lekin jab kisi lafz se 'koi' ya 'ek' murad lena ho toh (الْـ) hata diya jata hai. Baghair (الْـ) ke lafz par teeno harkaat mein se koi bhi harkat aa sakti hai, iss se uske maani par koi asar nahi padta. Harkaat ke bajaye lafz aur uske maani par tawajjoh dete hue, darj zail alfaaz ke maani samjhein aur likhein:"}},{"id":"sec_s1l13_g4","type":"two_col_numbered_list","data":{"is_numbered":false,"items":[{"id":"s1l13_g4_w1","arabic":"مَغْفِرَةٌ","arabic_markup":"<span class=\"arabic-root\">مَغْفِرَة</span><span class=\"nonroot\">ٌ</span>","hinglish":"Ek maghfirat / Bakhshish","translations":{"en":"A forgiveness / Any forgiveness","ur":"ایک مغفرت / بخشش","hi":"एक मग़फ़िरत / बख़्शिश"}},{"id":"s1l13_g4_w2","arabic":"رَحْمَةٌ","arabic_markup":"<span class=\"arabic-root\">رَحْمَةٌ</span>","hinglish":"Ek rehmat / Koi rehmat","translations":{"en":"A mercy / Any mercy","ur":"ایک رحمت / کوئی رحمت","hi":"एक रेहमत / कोई रेहमत"}},{"id":"s1l13_g4_w3","arabic":"قُرْآنٌ","arabic_markup":"<span class=\"arabic-root\">قُرْآن</span><span class=\"nonroot\">ٌ</span>","hinglish":"Ek Quran / Koi Quran","translations":{"en":"A Quran / Any Quran","ur":"ایک قرآن / کوئی قرآن","hi":"एक क़ुरआन / कोई क़ुरआन"}},{"id":"s1l13_g4_w4","arabic":"رَسُولٌ","arabic_markup":"<span class=\"arabic-root\">رَسُولٌ</span>","hinglish":"Ek Rasool / Koi Rasool","translations":{"en":"A Messenger / Any Messenger","ur":"ایک رسول / کوئی رسول","hi":"एक रसूल / कोई रसूल"}},{"id":"s1l13_g4_w5","arabic":"حَقٌّ","arabic_markup":"<span class=\"arabic-root\">حَقّ</span><span class=\"nonroot\">ٌ</span>","hinglish":"Ek haq / Sach","translations":{"en":"A truth / Right","ur":"ایک حق / سچ","hi":"एक हक़ / सच"}},{"id":"s1l13_g4_w6","arabic":"حَسْرَةٌ","arabic_markup":"<span class=\"arabic-root\">حَسْرَة</span><span class=\"nonroot\">ٌ</span>","hinglish":"Ek hasrat / Afsos","translations":{"en":"A regret / Sorrow","ur":"ایک حسرت / افسوس","hi":"एक हसरत / अफ़सोस"}},{"id":"s1l13_g4_w7","arabic":"شَكٌّ","arabic_markup":"<span class=\"arabic-root\">شَكّ</span><span class=\"nonroot\">ٌ</span>","hinglish":"Ek shak / Koi shak","translations":{"en":"A doubt / Any doubt","ur":"ایک شک / کوئی شک","hi":"एक शक / कोई शक"}},{"id":"s1l13_g4_w8","arabic":"نِعْمَةٌ","arabic_markup":"<span class=\"arabic-root\">نِعْمَةٌ</span>","hinglish":"Ek ne'mat / Koi ne'mat","translations":{"en":"A blessing / Any favor","ur":"ایک نعمت / کوئی نعمت","hi":"एक नेअमत / कोई नेअमत"}},{"id":"s1l13_g4_w9","arabic":"مَالٌ","arabic_markup":"<span class=\"arabic-root\">مَال</span><span class=\"nonroot\">ٌ</span>","hinglish":"Ek maal / Daulat","translations":{"en":"A wealth / Any property","ur":"ایک مال / دولت","hi":"एक माल / दौलत"}},{"id":"s1l13_g4_w10","arabic":"عِلْمٌ","arabic_markup":"<span class=\"arabic-root\">عِلْمٌ</span>","hinglish":"Ek ilm / Koi ilm","translations":{"en":"A knowledge / Any knowledge","ur":"ایک علم / کوئی علم","hi":"एक इल्म / कोई इल्म"}},{"id":"s1l13_g4_w11","arabic":"شَيْءٌ","arabic_markup":"<span class=\"arabic-root\">شَيْء</span><span class=\"nonroot\">ٌ</span>","hinglish":"Ek cheez / Koi cheez","translations":{"en":"A thing / Anything","ur":"ایک چیز / کوئی چیز","hi":"एक चीज़ / कोई चीज़"}},{"id":"s1l13_g4_w12","arabic":"فِتْنَةٌ","arabic_markup":"<span class=\"arabic-root\">فِتْنَة</span><span class=\"nonroot\">ٌ</span>","hinglish":"Ek aazmaish / Fitna","translations":{"en":"A trial / Affliction","ur":"ایک آزمائش / فتنہ","hi":"एक आज़माइश / फ़ितना"}},{"id":"s1l13_g4_w13","arabic":"ذِلَّةٌ","arabic_markup":"<span class=\"arabic-root\">ذِلَّة</span><span class=\"nonroot\">ٌ</span>","hinglish":"Ek zillat / Ruswaai","translations":{"en":"A humiliation / Disgrace","ur":"ایک ذلت / رسوائی","hi":"एक ज़िल्लत / रुसवाई"}},{"id":"s1l13_g4_w14","arabic":"غَضَبٌ","arabic_markup":"<span class=\"arabic-root\">غَضَبٌ</span>","hinglish":"Ek gussa / Ghazab","translations":{"en":"A wrath / Anger","ur":"ایک غضب / غصہ","hi":"एक ग़ज़ब / ग़ुस्सा"}},{"id":"s1l13_g4_w15","arabic":"فَضْلٌ","arabic_markup":"<span class=\"arabic-root\">فَضْل</span><span class=\"nonroot\">ٌ</span>","hinglish":"Ek fazal / Meharbaani","translations":{"en":"A bounty / Grace","ur":"ایک فضل / مہربانی","hi":"एक फ़ज़ल / मेहरबानी"}},{"id":"s1l13_g4_w16","arabic":"فَتْحٌ","arabic_markup":"<span class=\"arabic-root\">فَتْح</span><span class=\"nonroot\">ٌ</span>","hinglish":"Ek fatah / Kamyabi","translations":{"en":"A victory / Conquest","ur":"ایک فتح / کامیابی","hi":"एक फ़तह / कामयाबी"}},{"id":"s1l13_g4_w17","arabic":"رِزْقٌ","arabic_markup":"<span class=\"arabic-root\">رِزْقٌ</span>","hinglish":"Ek rizq / Rozi","translations":{"en":"A provision / Sustenance","ur":"ایک رزق / روزی","hi":"एक रिज़्क़ / रोज़ी"}},{"id":"s1l13_g4_w18","arabic":"أَجْرٌ","arabic_markup":"<span class=\"arabic-root\">أَجْر</span><span class=\"nonroot\">ٌ</span>","hinglish":"Ek ajr / Badla","translations":{"en":"A reward / Recompense","ur":"ایک اجر / بدلہ","hi":"एक अज्र / बदला"}},{"id":"s1l13_g4_w19","arabic":"ضَلَالٌ","arabic_markup":"<span class=\"arabic-root\">ضَلَال</span><span class=\"nonroot\">ٌ</span>","hinglish":"Ek gumraahi / Bhatakna","translations":{"en":"An error / Going astray","ur":"ایک گمراہی / بھٹکنا","hi":"एक गुमराही / भटकना"}},{"id":"s1l13_g4_w20","arabic":"هُدًى","arabic_markup":"<span class=\"arabic-root\">هُد</span><span class=\"nonroot\">ً</span><span class=\"arabic-root\">ى</span>","hinglish":"Ek hidayat / Rehnumaai","translations":{"en":"A guidance / Any guidance","ur":"ایک ہدایت / رہنمائی","hi":"एक हिदायत / रहनुमाई"}},{"id":"s1l13_g4_w21","arabic":"شِفَاءٌ","arabic_markup":"<span class=\"arabic-root\">شِفَاء</span><span class=\"nonroot\">ٌ</span>","hinglish":"Ek shifa / Ilaj","translations":{"en":"A healing / Cure","ur":"ایک شفا / علاج","hi":"एक शिफ़ा / इलाज"}},{"id":"s1l13_g4_w22","arabic":"مَرَضٌ","arabic_markup":"<span class=\"arabic-root\">مَرَض</span><span class=\"nonroot\">ٌ</span>","hinglish":"Ek beemari / Maraz","translations":{"en":"A disease / Illness","ur":"ایک مرض / بیماری","hi":"एक मर्ज़ / बीमारी"}},{"id":"s1l13_g4_w23","arabic":"مُصِيبَةٌ","arabic_markup":"<span class=\"arabic-root\">مُصِيبَة</span><span class=\"nonroot\">ٌ</span>","hinglish":"Ek museebat / Aafat","translations":{"en":"A calamity / Disaster","ur":"ایک مصیبت / آفت","hi":"एक मुसीबत / आफ़त"}},{"id":"s1l13_g4_w24","arabic":"عَهْدٌ","arabic_markup":"<span class=\"arabic-root\">عَهْد</span><span class=\"nonroot\">ٌ</span>","hinglish":"Ek waada / Mu'aahida","translations":{"en":"A covenant / Promise","ur":"ایک عہد / وعدہ","hi":"एक अहद / वादा"}},{"id":"s1l13_g4_w25","arabic":"عَدُوٌّ","arabic_markup":"<span class=\"arabic-root\">عَدُوّ</span><span class=\"nonroot\">ٌ</span>","hinglish":"Ek dushman / K